docs {
  # List categories

  Returns the product categories that currently hold at least one product.
  Backs the category filter chips of the mobile Catalog view; any client can
  use a category's `slug` as the `category` parameter of
  `GET /api/v1/catalog`.

  Categories come from the same external demo feed as the products
  (`https://api.escuelajs.co/api/v1/categories`). That feed accepts writes
  from anyone, so the server drops categories with no products and caps how
  many it inspects.

  ## Caching

  The list is cached in process for **5 minutes**. A failed lookup is never
  cached and never evicts a still-valid entry.

  ## Auth

  None. This endpoint is public.

  ## Parameters

  None.

  ## Responses

  ### 200 OK

  {
    "categories": [
      { "id": 1, "name": "Clothes", "slug": "clothes" }
    ]
  }

  - `categories` (array) — in feed order.
  - `categories[].id` (number) — feed identifier.
  - `categories[].name` (string) — display name.
  - `categories[].slug` (string) — URL-safe identifier; pass it to `/catalog`.

  ### 502 Bad Gateway — category source unavailable

  The feed is unreachable, timed out, or answered a non-2xx status.

  {
    "statusCode": 502,
    "error": "Bad Gateway",
    "message": "The category source is unavailable.",
    "validation": [],
    "url": "/api/v1/categories",
    "method": "GET"
  }
}
